  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Kimi-K3-inspired architecture release, plus paged serving for every attention type. BREAKING (source-level, F# consumers): new fields on ModelConfig (hybridAttention, attnRes), MoeConfig (router, latentDim) and TrainingConfig (mtpLossMode) break FULL record literals — use `{ ModelConfigs.dev with ... }`; new union cases (ActivationType.SiTUGLU, AttentionType.KDA, OptimizerConfig.Muon, KvCache.KdaCache/HybridCache) make downstream exhaustive matches incomplete. Standalone model-config.json files no longer need explicit nulls for unused optional sections. ARCHITECTURE: Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) linear attention with lower-bounded decay and NoPE; per-layer hybrid layouts (K3's 3:1 KDA/MLA, `--attention kda-hybrid`); Stable LatentMoE (routed experts in a latent space with RMSNorm before the up-projection); SiTU-GLU softcapped activation; sigmoid MoE routing with a frozen selection bias imported from donor e_score_correction_bias; Quantile Balancing (aux-loss-free load balancing); Block Attention Residuals (experimental; dense uniform attention, training/uncached-eval only); Muon optimizer with a per-head variant (`--optimizer muon`, `--muon-per-head`); EAGLE-3-style LK acceptance-rate loss for MTP draft heads (`--mtp-loss lk`). Wizard flags for all of it (`--situglu`, `--moe-router`, `--moe-latent-dim`, `--attnres`). SERVING: the paged KV pool now carries a per-layer page shape, so continuous batching covers MLA and per-layer hybrid (MLA's compressed-latent pages are smaller, so the same memory budget buys more concurrency) and KDA (whose fixed-size recurrent state lives in a per-sequence side table costing no pages). Optional cross-request KDA prefix-state checkpointing (`FUUGA_KDA_PREFIX_CACHE`, off by default). Paged scratch caches now follow the model dtype, fixing bf16/fp16 checkpoints on the per-sequence path. `FUUGA_PAGED_DISABLE` is a temporary rollback switch. BEHAVIOUR CHANGES worth reading before upgrading: (1) MoE generation now attends to full history — MoE blocks previously had no cached forward, so token-by-token decoding attended only to the current token; existing MoE checkpoints will produce different (correct) text. (2) Expert capacity is now training-only and its formula gained the missing activeExperts factor, so no tokens are dropped at inference and MoE training drops far fewer assignments. DONOR IMPORT: Kimi K3 (`--mapping kimi-k3`) with MXFP4 auto-dequantization, the documented `--moe-start-layer/--moe-end-layer/--moe-donor-experts/--moe-selected-experts` flags, and `deepseek-moe` as a real mapping. Exports refuse configurations they cannot represent (SiTU-GLU, AttnRes, hybrid layouts) instead of emitting a silently different model. FIXES: speculative decoding falls back safely for KDA layouts instead of corrupting recurrent state; MoE with a non-GQA attention type is rejected rather than silently running GQA; Newton-Schulz orthogonalization no longer builds the Gram matrix on the larger dimension; a KV-cache swap snapshot could alias and be zeroed on CPU pools. Test suite is now deterministic (private RNG generators, pinned OpenMP threads) and runs faster. Two new examples: examples/k3-style-architecture.fsx and examples/continuous-batching-and-paged-cache.fsx.",
